---
import InfoPage from '../layouts/InfoPage.astro';
---
<InfoPage title="Privacy" description="What the Fatt Pundit website collects (very little) and why." kicker="Short and plain" heading="Privacy"
  summary={[
    'No advertising cookies or trackers, so no cookie banner.',
    'We count visits without cookies or personal data.',
    'What you send us (an enquiry, the Dubai list) is used only to answer you, and deleted on request.',
  ]}>
  <p>This website doesn't use advertising cookies or trackers, and doesn't need a cookie banner.</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Visit counts.</strong> We count page views with a privacy-friendly tool that stores no cookies and no personal data: no IP addresses, no profiles.</li>
    <li><strong>Page speed.</strong> Your browser reports how fast pages loaded (numbers only), so we can keep the site quick.</li>
    <li><strong>Things you tell us.</strong> If you send an enquiry or join our list, we keep your name, email and message only to answer you or send the news you asked for. You can ask us to delete them at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>On this device.</strong> We remember the restaurant you last chose and your dish passport in your browser's own storage. It never leaves your device.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Bookings</h2>
  <p>Table bookings are made with OpenTable (Soho) and SevenRooms (Covent Garden), under their privacy policies.</p>
  {(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_FORM_ENDPOINT || import.meta.env.PUBLIC_DUBAI_LIST_ENDPOINT) && <p>Group enquiries and Dubai list sign-ups reach us by email through a form service, which passes them on to the restaurant.</p>}
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or deletion requests: <a href="mailto:reservations@fattpundit.co.uk">reservations@fattpundit.co.uk</a>.</p>
  <p class="todo">Draft: the company name, registered address and data controller details to be added by Fatt Pundit before launch.</p>
</InfoPage>
